  "loop_card": {
    "text": "Why do we sleep?",
    "cue": "next",
    "left": "😴",
    "right": "🌙"
  },
  "lines": [
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Dad, why do I have to go to sleep? I'm not even tired!",
      "board": {
        "type": "title",
        "left": {
          "icon": "😴",
          "label": "Sleep"
        },
        "right": {
          "icon": "🤔",
          "label": "Why?"
        },
        "mid": "?"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Great question! Tonight we'll find out what your body and brain do while you sleep, and why it matters so much.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🌙",
        "text": "Body and brain at night",
        "cue": "body",
        "sub": "Why sleep matters",
        "sub_cue": "matters"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Do they do anything? I'm just lying there!"
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "They're busier than you think! First: sleep is like plugging in a tablet to charge. All day you use up energy, and sleep fills you back up.",
      "chapter": "Recharge time",
      "punch": "charge",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🔋",
        "text": "Recharge time!",
        "cue": "charge",
        "sub": "Fill up your energy",
        "sub_cue": "energy"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "So I'm like a robot with a battery?"
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Kind of! But even cooler. While you sleep, your body does lots of fixing and growing.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🛠️",
        "text": "Fixing and growing",
        "cue": "fixing"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Growing? While I'm asleep?"
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Yes! In deep sleep, your body makes a special helper called growth hormone. So you really do grow while you sleep!",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "📏",
        "text": "You grow while you sleep!",
        "cue": "growth"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "So if I sleep all week, I'll be as tall as you!"
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Ha! It happens slowly, a tiny bit at a time. Sleep also helps your muscles get stronger and helps your body fight off germs.",
      "board": {
        "type": "gallery",
        "title": "Sleep helps you",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "📏",
            "label": "Grow slowly",
            "cue": "slowly"
          },
          {
            "icon": "img:Human_physiology/Servier/muscle-1",
            "label": "Strong muscles",
            "cue": "muscles"
          },
          {
            "icon": "img:Microbiology/Servier/bacterium",
            "label": "Fight germs",
            "cue": "germs"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "What does my brain do at night?",
      "chapter": "Your busy brain"
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "It's like a librarian! It sorts through what you learned today and stores the important things, so you remember them tomorrow.",
      "punch": "librarian",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "img:Human_physiology/Servier/brain-1",
        "text": "Sorting memories",
        "cue": "sorts",
        "sub": "Storing what matters",
        "sub_cue": "stores"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "So sleeping makes me smarter?"
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "It helps a lot! When you sleep well, it's easier to learn, pay attention and remember things.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🎒",
        "text": "Easier to learn",
        "cue": "learn",
        "sub": "And to remember",
        "sub_cue": "remember"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Does my brain clean up too?"
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Scientists think so! They think your brain washes away waste while you sleep, like tidying your room at the end of the day.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🧹",
        "text": "A brain clean-up",
        "cue": "washes",
        "sub": "Like tidying your room",
        "sub_cue": "tidying"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Is sleep the same all night long?",
      "chapter": "Sleep stages and dreams"
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "No! Sleep comes in stages. First light sleep, then deep sleep, then dream sleep. Then it starts again.",
      "board": {
        "type": "cycle",
        "title": "Sleep cycle",
        "center": "🌙",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "😌",
            "label": "Light sleep",
            "cue": "light"
          },
          {
            "icon": "😴",
            "label": "Deep sleep",
            "cue": "deep"
          },
          {
            "icon": "💭",
            "label": "Dream sleep",
            "cue": "dream"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "How many times does it go around?"
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Several times every night, round and round, like a merry-go-round.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🎠",
        "text": "Several rounds a night",
        "cue": "several"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "When do I have dreams?"
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Most dreams happen in dream sleep. Your eyes even dart around under your eyelids, as if you're watching a movie!",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "👀",
        "text": "Eyes dart around",
        "cue": "eyes",
        "sub": "Watching a dream",
        "sub_cue": "watching"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Why do we dream, though?"
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "That's still a mystery! Scientists think dreams might help your brain sort out feelings and memories. They're still finding out.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "💭",
        "text": "Still a mystery!",
        "cue": "mystery",
        "sub": "Scientists are curious",
        "sub_cue": "scientists"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "What does my body do in deep sleep?"
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "It gets super calm. Your breathing slows down, and your heart beats slow and steady.",
      "board": {
        "type": "body",
        "title": "Calm body",
        "show": [
          "lungs",
          "heart"
        ],
        "flow": "air",
        "cue": "breathing",
        "labels": [
          {
            "text": "Slow breaths",
            "at": "lungs",
            "cue": "slows"
          },
          {
            "text": "Calm heart",
            "at": "heart",
            "cue": "heart"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Do animals sleep too?",
      "chapter": "Sleepy animals"
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Lots of them do! A koala can snooze in a tree for up to about 20 hours a day.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🐨",
        "text": "Koalas: sleepyheads!",
        "cue": "koala",
        "sub": "Up to about 20 hours",
        "sub_cue": "20"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Twenty hours? Lucky koala!"
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Giraffes sleep only a few hours, often in short naps. And dolphins rest half their brain at a time, so they can keep swimming.",
      "board": {
        "type": "compare",
        "left": {
          "label": "Giraffes",
          "items": [
            {
              "icon": "🦒",
              "text": "Short naps",
              "cue": "short"
            }
          ]
        },
        "right": {
          "label": "Dolphins",
          "items": [
            {
              "icon": "🐬",
              "text": "Half a brain",
              "cue": "half"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Half a brain? That's so weird and cool!"
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "And kids need more sleep than grown-ups: often 10 hours or even more!",
      "board": {
        "type": "compare",
        "left": {
          "label": "Kids",
          "items": [
            {
              "icon": "🧒",
              "text": "More sleep",
              "cue": "kids"
            }
          ]
        },
        "right": {
          "label": "Grown-ups",
          "items": [
            {
              "icon": "🧑",
              "text": "Less sleep",
              "cue": "grown"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "What happens if I don't get enough sleep?",
      "chapter": "Good sleep tips"
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "You might feel grumpy, tired and wobbly. It's harder to think, play and get along with friends.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "😫",
        "text": "Grumpy and tired",
        "cue": "grumpy",
        "sub": "Harder to think",
        "sub_cue": "harder"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "That's me after a sleepover!"
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Ha! Here's a cool trick: when it gets dark, your brain makes a sleepy signal. It tells your body: time for bed!",
      "board": {
        "type": "journey",
        "title": "Getting sleepy",
        "traveler": "🌙",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "🌆",
            "label": "It gets dark",
            "cue": "dark"
          },
          {
            "icon": "img:Human_physiology/Servier/brain-1",
            "label": "Sleepy signal",
            "cue": "sleepy"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🛏️",
            "label": "Time for bed!",
            "cue": "bed"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Is that why screens before bed are a bad idea?"
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Yes! Bright screens can trick your brain into thinking it's still daytime. So switch them off a while before bed.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "📱",
        "text": "Screens off before bed",
        "cue": "screens",
        "sub": "They trick your brain",
        "sub_cue": "trick"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "What else helps?"
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Go to bed at the same time each night, have a warm bath, read a calm story, and keep your room dark and cozy.",
      "board": {
        "type": "checklist",
        "title": "Good sleep",
        "icon": "🌙",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "⏰",
            "text": "Same bedtime",
            "cue": "same",
            "ok": true
          },
          {
            "icon": "🛁",
            "text": "Warm bath",
            "cue": "bath",
            "ok": true
          },
          {
            "icon": "📖",
            "text": "Calm story",
            "cue": "story",
            "ok": true
          },
          {
            "icon": "🌑",
            "text": "Dark, cozy room",
            "cue": "dark",
            "ok": true
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "And a cuddly teddy!",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🧸",
        "text": "A cuddly teddy!",
        "cue": "teddy"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Quiz time! Question one: in which kind of sleep do most dreams happen? Think...",
      "chapter": "Quiz time",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "❓",
        "text": "Quiz time!",
        "cue": "quiz",
        "sub": "Where are dreams?",
        "sub_cue": "dreams"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Dream sleep!",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "💭",
        "text": "Dream sleep!",
        "cue": "dream"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Yes! Question two: which animal can rest half its brain at a time? Think...",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🤔",
        "text": "Half-brain sleeper?",
        "cue": "half"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "The dolphin!",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🐬",
        "text": "The dolphin!",
        "cue": "dolphin"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Right! Last one: do kids need more sleep or less sleep than grown-ups? Think...",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "⚖️",
        "text": "More or less?",
        "cue": "more"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "More sleep! So I can grow!",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🧒",
        "text": "More sleep!",
        "cue": "more"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Super! So sleep recharges your energy, helps you grow, saves what you learned, and helps you feel happy.",
      "board": {
        "type": "summary",
        "rows": [
          {
            "icon": "🔋",
            "text": "Recharge energy",
            "cue": "recharges"
          },
          {
            "icon": "📏",
            "text": "Grow",
            "cue": "grow"
          },
          {
            "icon": "img:Human_physiology/Servier/brain-1",
            "text": "Save memories",
            "cue": "saves"
          },
          {
            "icon": "😊",
            "text": "Feel happy",
            "cue": "happy"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Okay, okay... I'll go to bed. Good night, Dad!",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🌙",
        "text": "Good night!",
        "cue": "night"
      }
    },
    {
